  "response_text": "If we don\u2019t set the Process Stack Pointer (PSP) using __set_PSP before running a new thread, the CPU won\u2019t know where that thread\u2019s stack is located. Since every function relies on the stack for things like storing return addresses and local variables, using an uninitialized or incorrect PSP causes the CPU to access invalid memory. This triggers a hard fault, which is the processor\u2019s way of handling critical errors like invalid memory access. Setting the PSP ensures the new thread has a valid stack to operate on, preventing the system from crashing.\\n",
